  "id": "DrugBank_DB00635 - MONDO_grouped_6545_44719",
  "verbalization": "Prednisone is implicated in the pathogenesis of Erythema Multiforme through a mechanism involving glucocorticoid receptor activation. The evidence suggests that Prednisone, through its indication for Fetal Erythroblastosis, Chronic Beryllium Disease, and Familial Glucocorticoid Deficiency, ultimately leads to Erythema Multiforme via Dexamethasone, a glucocorticoid. This chain of indications implies a potential role of glucocorticoids in the development of Erythema Multiforme, possibly through immunomodulatory effects. The overlapping pathways highlight a shared dependency on glucocorticoids, suggesting that the condition may be influenced by the dysregulation of glucocorticoid signaling. The evidence supports a mechanism where Prednisone, through its glucocorticoid activity, contributes to the manifestation of Erythema Multiforme, though the exact molecular pathways remain to be fully elucidated.",
